  "task_instruction": "Implement the minimap logic: export a Player reference and a zoom property with a clamped setter, cache the grid and marker prototypes, center the player marker after the first frame, compute grid_scale from the grid size and viewport, duplicate and show markers for every node in the minimap_objects group using their minimap_icon keys, store them in a 'markers' dictionary, rotate (player rotation + PI/2) and position markers each frame relative to the player (scaling to 0.75 and clamping when off the grid), implement _on_object_removed which removes and erases markers when called, and implement _on_gui_input which handles mouse wheel gui_input to adjust zoom. Ensure the world scene connects minimap_objects \"removed\" signals to the minimap while mobs/crates have the \"removed\" signals, expose each one's \"minimap_icon\", and ensure mobs/crates belong to the minimap_objects group.",
